The main focus of this paper is to examine multiple solution possibilities for a specific Kirchhoff type elliptic system of equations given by (1.1), particularly in identifying conditions under which solutions with given characteristics can be found. This system involves functions $u$ and $v$ satisfying the equations \begin{align*}
  -\Delta _a u &=\left( au^{p-1}+b\left( \int _{\Omega }|u|^{q}dx\right) ^{p/q}-\lambda \right) _+u^{p-1} \\
  -\Delta _a v &=\left( av^{p-1}+b\left( \int _{\Omega }|v|^{q}dx\right) ^{p/q}-\lambda \right) _+v^{p-1}
\end{align*}where $\Delta _a u =\text {div} \left( a(x)\nabla u\right)$, $a\in {\mathcal {A}}(\Omega )$, $q>1$, $p\in \left( 1,\frac{q}{q-1}\right)$ and the singular Trudinger-Moser critical theory is applied to solve these equations.
